cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Warrant: transitions of work, exact closures and what remains open"
abstract: >-
  An agent protocol for recording transitions of work with their residual. A
  transition says what was done, on what basis, what it established, which exact
  conditions it closes, which questions it opens and what it leaves
  unestablished. Assessment of one immutable view answers whether a present use
  may rely on a closure, what is open for whom, and what the next session needs.
  Computation conditions are credited only by the recipient's own replay with a
  pinned Sigma-GLYPH kernel. Warrant 0.x (signed decision records with re-runnable
  reasons) is preserved at the tag history/warrant-0.x-2026-10-18.
message: "If you use or evaluate this work, please cite it."
type: software
license: MIT
